        <headline>Flash Flood Warning issued September 25 at 2:56PM MDT until September 25 at 4:30PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</headline>
        <description>At 256 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated the heaviest rainfall has
ended across the warned area. Up to 1.25 inches of rain have fallen
in the area between Casa Blanca Road, Marmon Ranch Road, and Sunset
Road east of Acoma Pueblo and south of Laguna Pueblo. Additional
rainfall amounts up to 0.50 inches are possible with the next batch
of showers and thunderstorms. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected
to begin shortly.

HAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing
flash flooding.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban
areas, highways, streets and underpasses.

Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...
Laguna Pueblo, New Laguna, Mesita, Acoma Pueblo, Paraje, Seama and
Acomita.

This includes Interstate 40 between Mile Markers 106 and 122.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Be aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.</instruction>
